.TH HEE_STATUS 3 "2026-09-01" "HEE" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
hee_status \- emit a status line in the org vocabulary (shell and Python)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SS Shell
.nf
. "$TOOL_ROOT/library/bash/vis.status.shfn.bash"

hee_status LEVEL MESSAGE...
hee_status_code LEVEL
hee_status_demo
hee_link TEXT URL
hee_link_issue REPO NUMBER
.fi
.SS Python
.nf
from hee_status import status, render, emit, demo
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Two implementations of one vocabulary \(em see
.BR hee-status (7)
for the levels and what they mean. They are kept in lockstep deliberately:
a shell tool and a Python tool reporting the same condition must produce
identical text, or a parser downstream of both has to special\-case which
wrote the line.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B hee_status " LEVEL MESSAGE..."
Emit one status line in the current
.BR HEE_STATUS_STYLE .
.TP
.B hee_status_code " LEVEL"
Print the Nagios exit code for a level. Use as
.BR "exit $(hee_status_code CRITICAL)" ,
never a hardcoded integer.
.TP
.B hee_status_demo
Render every level in every style. For choosing a preference.
.TP
.B hee_link " TEXT URL"
An OSC 8 terminal hyperlink when stdout is a TTY, degrading to
.I text <url>
when it is not. Measured 2026\-08\-31: OSC 8 works from a tool writing to a
TTY, but is stripped in transit from an agent's chat output.
.TP
.B hee_link_issue " REPO NUMBER"
The same, for an issue or PR reference.
.SH PARITY
.I tests/status-parity.sh
runs 21 inputs across all three styles through both implementations and
fails if they disagree.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hee-status (7),
.BR heerc (5)
